Project Title
  Bakery Shop Ingredients Inventory

Problem Statement
  Taking inventory of the ingredients in bakeshops with pen and paper is exhausting, sluggish, and susceptible to errors simply because of human nature. Maybe the person taking inventory is tired from work, or they rush 
  the work too much that it becomes faulty. With this program, the process becomes quick, easy, and accurate, saving time and energy. This program allows any employee to record every change in the stock of ingredients. 
  As of now, the 18 ingredients are: yeast, white sugar, brown sugar, water, butter, eggs, flour, milk, chocolate filling, vanilla filling, strawberry filling, salt, raisins, cinnamon, cream, walnuts, peanuts, cheese 
  and condensed milk. This program could be updated mid-shift every time an ingredient is used and measured, or at the end of the day.

Project Objectives
  >> This project aims to help employees of a bakery to keep track of their ingredients. It shows them if something needs restocking, helping with resource management.
  >> Counting and measuring every ingredient in a bakery at the end of the day is tedious and lengthy. If it was quickly updated during work hours, it would be much easier.
  >> The ingredients may be replaced with other easily available things for testing.
  >> Computer programs make zero mistakes as long as the data is properly given. The program heavily reduces effort needed to calculate the stock and increases accuracy.
  >> This project must be completed within the school year.

Planned Features
  1.Start the program
  2.Ask for required ingredients.
  3.Track the ammounts of ingredients left.
  4.Output the ammounts and remind the user what was left.
  

Planned Inputs and Outputs
  Inputs:
    yeast, white sugar, brown sugar, water, butter, eggs, flour, milk, chocolate filling, vanilla filling, strawberry filling, salt, raisins, cinnamon, cream, walnuts, peanuts, cheese, condensed milk, repeat

  Output:
    "All clear!"
    "WARNING! You have only 500 mL of water left."
    "WARNING! You have no eggs left."

Logic Plan
  1. START
  2. Set the current measurements of the ingredients
  3. Update the stocks of each ingredient at the end of each day, or alternatively as the ingredients are being used
  4. If the updated stock is low, warn the user
  5. If the updated stock is empty, tell the user
  6. Once all stocks have been updated, ask the user if they would like to redo it (Y/N)
  7. If Y, loop back to step 2
  8. If N, end the program
